ief there are worries about what  the president might continue  to try to do do you share any of those  do you have any  links into the white house now do you  know the president's mood do you get a  sense of  whether he's given up we saw that video  he delivered on thursday evening  saying that the full force of the law  would be used against those that  attacked the capitol building some said  it seemed more like a hostage video  do you have any sense of the president's  mind at this point  i don't i have not spoken to him since  the events of last wednesday  i will say however that again i mean  impeachment is a political tool and  that's what is being used right now by  the democrats  i understand their desire to appease  their base but the reality is  that again we're nine days from this we  know the political outcome of either one  of these avenues that's available  and neither one of them produce an  outcome that's serious  so the reality is that by the day that  they actually get this thing moving  forward  the senate is not meeting again until  the 19th of january  right so that just shows you the reality  of the situation  that we know it's not going to happen so  you could be as concerned as you want  in theory but the reality is is that the  the legislative calendar doesn't allow  for this to occur  prior to the president leaving office at  noon on january 20th  and just your thoughts sean spicer on  what  the president was up to last wednesday  that extraordinary sequence of events  the speech he made to the crowd  then they marched on the capitol  building the lack of security  surrounding the capitol building in  particular federal  security none of that there it seems and  then none  called in for several hours and the  extraordinary letter  sent the day before by the 10 living  defense  secretaries warning the military not to  get involved do you think the president  actually made an attempt somehow  to get the military of the united states  of america to support his ambition to  stay in power  there's a lot to unpack in that question  and i mean i i think that  in the days and hopefully the months to  come we take a lot a lot and  hard look at each one of those things  particularly  the concern about security at the united  states capital we're seeing reports come  out today i haven't confirmed them  independently  that the police chief for the capitol  police  had asked for support from both the  house and the senate  uh sergeant-at-arms who oversees the  chamber security in both of the  respective  houses of congress you know that should  set red flags up why wasn't that call  for help  listened to or heated by those two  respective chambers  there's going to be a lot of look  especially as we head towards this  inauguration on january 20th  to make sure that the proper precautions  are being taken taking place  but but i i mean i will say this that as  an american  i you know if you had told me the day  before that fellow americans  were going to rush the capital of the  united states and break down barriers  and go through security and  break windows and harm people i i would  have told you that that was unfathomable  we haven't had attacks on our country  like that  in our history i mean they are from  outside they are  al qaeda attacking us um and an outside  interest attacking us on 9 11.  it you know you go back to japan  attacking us in world war ii  these are not things internal uh  threats that we have seen in our country  the likes of which we saw  last wednesday and so i i think it's  very difficult in some cases to look and  say how could you not have seen this  because we hadn't we never thought of it  as an american to think of another  american attacking  our own institutions in the way that  they were last wednesday is something  that if you had told me tuesday or  wednesday morning  you know i bet you these folks are going  to do this i would have said there's no  way  this isn't something 